        <h1 class="article-title">Vanishing Waters: How Unchecked Urbanization is Choking India's Wetland Ecosystems</h1>
        <div class="article-subtitle">
            Over one-third of India's natural wetlands have disappeared in recent decades under the bulldozer of urban expansion. From Bengaluru's inflammable foam lakes to Guwahati's toxic garbage dumps in Deepor Beel, an ecological tragedy is paving over the nation's vital natural infrastructure.
